  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe central idea is to use a particle swarm optimization (PSO) approach with specialized constraint handling to explore the solution space more thoroughly than gradient-based local search methods. This addresses the bottleneck of local optima by leveraging swarm intelligence for global search while maintaining feasibility through repair mechanisms. The PSO framework allows dynamic adjustment of particle positions based on both individual and swarm performance, enabling exploration of diverse candidate solutions that may outperform cluster-based or random initialization strategies. This approach is particularly suited to the non-convex, high-dimensional nature of the problem and avoids the pitfalls of getting trapped in suboptimal regions.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nThe step function h is represented as a vector h \u2208 [0,1]^n_points over [0,2] with dx = 2.0 / n_points. The objective is to minimize the maximum overlap integral:\nC\u2085 = max_k \u222b\u2080\u00b2 h(x)(1 - h(x+k)) dx \nThis translates to computing max(np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode=\"full\") * dx) over all lags k.\n\nConstraints:\n- 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i\n- \u2211h[i] = n_points / 2 (ensuring \u222bh dx = 1)\n\nThe PSO algorithm maintains a population of particles, where each particle represents a candidate solution. The objective function is evaluated using the provided evaluator, and feasibility is enforced through repair operations after position updates.\n\n3. Implementation procedure\na. Parent validation: If initial_h_values is provided, use it as the initial swarm. Otherwise, generate a random valid initial swarm.\nb. Initialization:\n   i. Generate 30 particles with h[i] \u2208 [0,1]\n   ii. Normalize each particle to ensure \u2211h[i] = n_points/2\nc. Optimization loop:\n   i. For each iteration (up to 600 seconds):\n      1. Evaluate fitness: compute max(np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode=\"full\") * dx)\n      2. Update personal best (pbest) for each particle\n      3. Update global best (gbest) among all particles\n      4. Adjust velocity and position for each particle using:\n         v[i] = \u03c9*v[i] + c\u2081*r\u2081*(pbest[i] - h[i]) + c\u2082*r\u2082*(gbest - h[i])\n         h[i] = h[i] + v[i]\n      5. Repair infeasible solutions:\n         - Clip values to [0,1]\n         - Normalize to \u2211h[i] = n_points/2\nd. Termination: Stop when time budget is exhausted or when no improvement is detected for 50 consecutive iterations.\ne. Return the best solution found during the process.\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\nDefault configuration:\n- n_points = 400\n- n_particles = 30\n- Inertia weight \u03c9 = 0.7\n- Cognitive coefficient c\u2081 = 1.5\n- Social coefficient c\u2082 = 1.5\n- Max iterations = 1000\n- Perturbation frequency = 100 iterations\n\nVariations:\n1. Adaptive inertia weight decay \u03c9 = 0.7 - 0.001*t\n2. Different cognitive/social coefficients (c\u2081=2.0, c\u2082=1.0)\n3. Changing n_particles to 50 for higher exploration\n4. Using the parent solution as a global best seed if available\n5. Adjusting the correlation calculation to include only valid lags\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\nTime allocation:\n- 95% of time to the optimization loop\n- 5% to final refinement\n\nRobustness measures:\n- Fallback to initial solution if PSO fails\n- Ensure all h[i] \u2208 [0,1] through clipping\n- Validate \u2211h == n_points/2 after every repair\n- If numerical instability occurs, reduce inertia weight and restart\n\n6. Validation and return contract\nFeasibility checks:\n- Verify all h[i] \u2208 [0,1]\n- Confirm \u2211h == n_points/2\n- Ensure the correlation computation matches the evaluator's method\n\nObjective validation:\n- Re-evaluate the best solution using the provided evaluator\n- Compare with previous best values to ensure improvement\n\nInterface requirements:\n- Return h_values as a list of floats\n- Provide c5_bound as the computed maximum overlap\n- Include n_points as the number of samples\n\nSanity checks:\n- Confirm the correlation calculation includes all lags\n- Ensure the normalization step maintains the integral constraint\n- Verify the returned h_values array has length n_points",
